	(text "Front-panel display\n\n\nI2C bus (shared with the analog board via CAT6 pair 2):\n  0x21  PCF8575 -- this board (LCD + LEDs + optional paddle)\n  0x20  PCF8575 -- analog board, relay drives          [not on this sheet]\n  0x36  MAX17048 -- Metro on-board fuel gauge          [not on this sheet]\n  0x37  I2C QT rotary -- STEP  (A0 jumper closed to move off 0x36 / MAX17048)\n  0x38  I2C QT rotary -- FUNC  (A1 jumper closed)\n  0x60  Si5351A VFO                                    [not on this sheet]\n  0x67  MCP4728 quad DAC (post-EEPROM reprogram from factory 0x60)\n                                                       [not on this sheet]\n\nParts to add here (vector board, behind LCD -- exact design TBD):\n  - Adafruit PCF8575 I2C 16-GPIO expander (PID 5904) at 0x20 -- drives\n    the LCD in 4-bit mode, reads the paddle (option 2 below), and\n    drives the front-panel status LEDs.\n  - 2x Adafruit I2C QT Rotary Encoder breakouts (PID 4991) at 0x37\n    (STEP) and 0x38 (FUNC), each carrying a Bourns PEC11-4 encoder\n    with pushbutton. Onboard seesaw SAMD09 handles quadrature\n    decoding + button debounce.\n  - Winstar WH2004A 20x4 character LCD (4-bit mode via the PCF8575).\n  - MBL-600 optical encoder (RS-422 differential -- wires straight\n    through the CAT6 to the main-board receiver on the interface\n    sheet; does NOT pass through the PCF8575).\n  - Front-panel LEDs (TX, fault, VFO-lock) on spare PCF8575 GPIO.\n  - Bypass caps at LCD Vcc (10 uF + 100 nF). The PCF8575 and QT\n    encoder breakouts have their own bypassing + I2C pull-ups\n    on-board.\n  - LCD contrast trim pot, backlight series resistor.\n\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 194.056 48.768 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fb997aab-58dd-49c9-a7ec-0822a6581487")
	)
